    {
      "object_id": "mathia_interpretation_8bde8658b3cf188bef7172a41efe634711f58cbc283a9bfeba10934f45903746",
      "object_role": "interpretation",
      "proposed_content": "The proof of the small-x corollary is compressed to a scale condition and a growth comparison: invoke Theorem 1.1, impose x <= T, and use Lemma 2.2's f(u) << u^(1/2+ε) bound. This gains a short route from the detailed theorem to the endpoint conclusion and an error better than equation (2) on the stated range, but the span omits the termwise estimates, so it does not establish which individual contributions the bound controls.",
