    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_8361c2083efd1a5562f8c7e7bee1a1d67096802c1b253ce4a8fc9cee966626c0",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The proof separates the pair-correlation correction into three components in equation (12), evaluates the third as a discrete cosine-weighted singular-series response in equation (13), and converts the complementary head and tail components into a common centered-error and sine-kernel representation in equations (14) and (16). Their shared terms can then cancel explicitly in equation (17) before (13) and (17) are recombined with (12).",
